## Scenarios

### diff context guard

#### guards malformed context values

- Verify: guards malformed context values
   - Expected: parse_context_or_default("10", 3i64) equals `10i64)  # oracle: 10i64 — a real context value parses`
   - Expected: parse_context_or_default("0", 3i64) equals `0i64)  # oracle: 0i64 — zero is a valid context`
   - Expected: parse_context_or_default("not-a-number", 3i64) equals `3i64)  # oracle: 3i64 — garbage is defaulted, not crashed on`
   - Expected: parse_context_or_default("3.5", 3i64) equals `3i64)  # oracle: 3i64 — fractional text is defaulted`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 7 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-APP-001
step("Verify: guards malformed context values")
# Runtime oracle: values as they arrive from a --context=<value> argument.
expect(parse_context_or_default("10", 3i64)).to_equal(10i64)  # oracle: 10i64 — a real context value parses
expect(parse_context_or_default("0", 3i64)).to_equal(0i64)  # oracle: 0i64 — zero is a valid context
expect(parse_context_or_default("not-a-number", 3i64)).to_equal(3i64)  # oracle: 3i64 — garbage is defaulted, not crashed on
expect(parse_context_or_default("3.5", 3i64)).to_equal(3i64)  # oracle: 3i64 — fractional text is defaulted
```

